78 #edb/ref 17592186418412 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592186418413 1079 #uuid "69ac052e-a374-5b6c-af86-f7bda6ec7c19" 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592186418414 1068 #edb/ref 17592186418413 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592186418414 1069 "q-84984" 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592186418414 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592186418414 1071 "A soccer coach must choose a defensive lineup for each of the $4$ defensive positions from a roster of $11$ defenders. How many potential starting defensive lineups are there?" 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592186418414 1072 #uuid "9a0bfa46-736f-571e-9fd1-af2e7c4186b1" 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592186418414 1074 "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $11$ defenders, so $n=11.$ We want to select $4$ of those defenders to play in each of the $4$ positions, so we have $r=4.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different starting defensive lineups is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{11}{P}_{4} & =\\frac{11!}{(11-4)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{11!}{7!} \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8\\cdot \\cancel{7!}}{\\cancel{7!}} \\\\  & =11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =7\\,920.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592186418415 1058 #edb/ref 17592186418416 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592186418415 1062 #uuid "4438f96a-bc01-54cd-950c-bb4c7070f017" 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592186418415 1063 #edb/ref 17592186394620 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592186418416 1062 #uuid "ef1e5084-9458-5f6f-93ee-c68edf6f4933" 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592186418416 1063 #edb/ref 17592186418414 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592186418417 1058 #edb/ref 17592186418415 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592186418417 1062 #uuid "fd11f4d8-2ca8-5342-ad46-6e479321ae16" 13194139534314 17592186045417 true] [17592